The ring of J.A.R.V.I.S's HUD (~/jarvis/bin/jarvis-hud-overlay) as
i3lock-color's unlock indicator, with --jarvis (bin/anthe-lock).

Built on i3lock-color e6c0caf (https://github.com/Raymo111/i3lock-color),
in ~/software/i3lock-color, installed as ~/.local/bin/i3lock-color:

    git apply ~/.dotfiles/rcfiles/i3lock/jarvis-ring.patch
    autoreconf -fi && mkdir -p build && cd build
    ../configure --prefix=$HOME/.local --disable-sanitizers && make
    cp i3lock ~/.local/bin/i3lock-color

It needs /etc/pam.d/i3lock, from Ubuntu's i3lock package (apt install i3lock),
with only, so that a wrong password is refused at once:

    auth required pam_unix.so nodelay

